"label":"GDP per head","value":45918,"year":"2023","kind":"gbp"},{"label":"Band D council tax (area bill)","value":2442.66,"year":"2026-27","kind":"gbp"},{"label":"Band D \u2014 council's own element","value":241.28,"year":"2026-27","kind":"gbp"}]}},"dossier":{"summary":{"summary":"South Ribble is effectively debt-free: gross debt at 31 March 2026 was just \u00a342k of finance leases, with the \u00a325.1m capital financing requirement met entirely from the council's own cash and no external borrowing taken in the year. Investments stood at \u00a322.3m at year end (average daily balance \u00a337.1m, earning \u00a31,503k at 3.63%), including \u00a311m of term deposits with Blackpool and Bournemouth, Christchurch & Poole councils, and financing costs are a modest 3.28% of the net revenue stream. The trend to watch is slow cash erosion: average balances fell 16.6% year-on-year and interest earned dropped 33% as capital spending is funded internally, while the CFR rose from \u00a319.7m to \u00a325.1m. All prudential indicators and counterparty limits were complied with.","fy":"2025/26","as_of_doc":"Treasury Management Outturn Report 2025/26","as_of_url":"https://southribble.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s57901/Treasury Management Outturn Report 202526 Committee report template.pdf","as_of_date":"2026-07-21","signals":[{"code":"none","headline":"Debt-free at 31 March 2026: \u00a342k gross debt (finance leases only) vs \u00a322.3m investments; no borrowing taken and all indicators complied","why":"Verified quiet \u2014 internal resources comfortably cover a \u00a325.1m CFR, though average cash fell 16.6% year-on-year as capital spend is funded internally."}],"key_figures":[{"name":"cfr","value":"\u00a325,126k closing (opening \u00a319,724k; original estimate \u00a333,356k)","as_at":"31/3/26","page":4},{"name":"borrowing","value":"gross debt \u00a342k \u2014 other long-term liabilities (finance leases) only; no external loans and none taken in year","as_at":"31 March 2026","pag